{"step_index":122,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-15T20:24:44Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-16T01:54:44+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-16T01:54:53+05:30\nThe search for \"\"whiteboard animation\" github cli python OR nodejs \"VideoScribe\" alternative stars\" returned the following summary:\nFor those seeking open-source alternatives to **VideoScribe** or looking to build programmatic whiteboard animations using Python or Node.js, several options exist on GitHub.\n\n### **Notable Open-Source Whiteboard Animation Tools**\n*   **[Inkplainer-OS](https://github.com/NadirWeb-App/Inkplainer-OS)**: A browser-based, open-source tool designed specifically as an alternative to VideoScribe and Doodly. It allows you to convert images and text into whiteboard-style explainer videos with multiple animation styles (e.g., hand-drawn reveal, contour, scanner) and exports to MP4/WebM[1][2].\n*   **[OpenDoodler](https://github.com/Rsverma/OpenDoodler)**: A C#/.NET-based desktop application that allows you to compose SVG and text graphics on a canvas, animate them stroke-by-stroke, and export the result as an MP4 video[3][4].\n\n### **Programmatic & AI-Driven Approaches**\nIf you prefer a CLI-based or programmatic approach, these projects leverage Python and computer vision:\n*   **[handanim](https://github.com/subroy13/handanim)**: A Python library that enables you to programmatically create whiteboard-style animations. It provides an API to animate hand-drawn diagrams, geometric shapes, and text, with exports to MP4 or SVG[5].\n*   **[whiteboard-animation-engine](https://github.com/haseebuchiha/whiteboard-animation-engine-first-video)**: A Python-based engine that automates the generation of explainer videos. It uses computer vision (SAM, GroundingDINO) to process images and create a \"hand-drawn\" animation pipeline[6].\n*   **[ai-img2sketch](https://github.com/daslearning-org/ai-img2sketch)**: A Python-based tool (with a Gradio UI) that converts images into whiteboard sketch animations using NumPy and OpenCV, without requiring heavy pre-trained models[7][8].\n\n### **Collaborative/Interactive Whiteboard Projects**\nIf your goal is building a real-time whiteboard (rather than an animation generator), many GitHub repositories focus on Node.js and React/Socket.io stacks:\n*   **[cracker0dks/whiteboard](https://github.com/cracker0dks/whiteboard)**: A lightweight, collaborative whiteboard app built with Node.js that supports real-time drawing, image drag-and-drop, and saving boards as JSON or images[9][10].\n*   **[Sync-Canvas-Editor](https://github.com/shahriar-ahmed-seam/Sync-Canvas-Editor)**: A collaborative whiteboard using CRDTs (Yjs), Next.js, and Node.js WebSockets for conflict-free real-time interaction[11][12].\n\n### **Summary of Options**\n| Category | Tool/Project | Primary Language | Use Case |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Animation Generator** | **Inkplainer-OS** | HTML/JS | Direct VideoScribe alternative[1] |\n| **Programmatic** | **handanim** | Python | Scripting whiteboard videos[5] |\n| **Automated** | **whiteboard-animation-engine** | Python | AI-assisted pipeline[6] |\n| **Collaborative** | **cracker0dks/whiteboard** | Node.js | Real-time shared whiteboard[10] |\n\nFor most users looking for a **VideoScribe alternative** that works locally without a complex coding setup, **Inkplainer-OS** is the most direct recommendation[1][2]. For developers wanting to build a custom automation pipeline, **handanim** offers the most structured Python API[5].\n\nSources:\n[1] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFthfRs5re4uVTks-KqRLco0wlA6ZngjrsdH5SqmPqcEMRZ1TKlZhIVoYlh8mgx-HHZ72fpQJJA6xsftLQvrQxqqkUrj4jvDNC5nlHVbSdy_QRo3n0cspXTKQeKaSy1SzX3e_M=)\n[2] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlvCxGL2qOOWzhNc4VpdLKRyEStTzVX1l-tIKdTGiRq-yvi_Nzxo0MpmbqkvuzlOfPStL7Hh46_fCtX7Pl_UOhD63CqmcuoTjzAI4DXX7MHM3jvQg8pMf4_yatM