{"step_index":123,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-15T20:24:44Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-16T01:54:44+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-16T01:54:58+05:30\nThe search for \"github \"manim\" whiteboard hand draw extension plugin\" returned the following summary:\nWhile there is no single \"official\" plugin exclusively for whiteboard hand-drawing in Manim, you can achieve this effect using built-in features or dedicated third-party libraries.\n\n### Built-in Manim Capabilities\nManim (Community Edition) has powerful native animations that simulate hand-drawing without needing extra plugins:\n*   **`Write()`**: This is the standard animation for simulating the hand-writing of text or hand-drawing of shapes/paths. It is designed specifically to make objects appear as if they are being drawn onto the screen[1][2].\n*   **`Create()`**: This animation incrementally reveals a vectorized object (VMobject), which is the foundation for most drawing effects in Manim[1][2].\n*   **`DrawBorderThenFill()`**: This animates the outline of a shape before filling it, which provides a clean, professional drawing effect[1][2].\n\n### Dedicated Libraries\nIf you are looking for a specific tool outside of the core library to handle \"hand-drawn\" (sketchy/human-style) aesthetics, consider:\n*   **[handanim](https://github.com/subroy13/handanim)**: This is a separate Python library specifically designed to create \"whiteboard-style, hand-drawn animations.\" It is built to animate hand-drawn diagrams, handwritten text, and human-style sketching, and it integrates concepts similar to those found in Manim[3].\n\n### Tips for \"Hand-Drawn\" Styles\n*   **Styling**: Achieving a true \"hand-drawn\" or \"ink-bleed\" look usually involves applying specific stroke properties or using custom SVG assets that have a sketchy appearance[4][5].\n*   **Visual Editors**: If you prefer a drag-and-drop interface over writing raw code, projects like **Manim Studio** or **Manim Motion Editor** allow you to visually place objects and animate them, which can make creating complex sequences easier than coding them manually from scratch[6][7].\n*   **Combined Workflow**: Many creators use a hybrid approach, using Manim for the mathematical precision of the animation and overlaying it with custom hand-drawn assets created in tools like Adobe Animate or other vector software[8].\n\nSources:\n[1] [manim.community](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQESK1J4sY4ZoO4h4lycSN7yGP7RnohukSpBk_c0UVw2ljhORwJliCeu3GKR2-xGrmVKR2SMpMEcraFcDkFTPz4_cuRDGy3u1bX_qK4f9f0aKWovv-hy-YvG5Yro3GHhrTkY8qfbmrBzJC6tCX-GA6YBq19m0eVMgI_TUVsEXu6cLX1Opj4=)\n[2] [manim.community](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQESK1J4sY4ZoO4h4lycSN7yGP7RnohukSpBk_c0UVw2ljhORwJliCeu3GKR2-xGrmVKR2SMpMEcraFcDkFTPz4_cuRDGy3u1bX_qK4f9f0aKWovv-hy-YvG5Yro3GHhrTkY8qfbmrBzJC6tCX-GA6YBq19m0eVMgI_TUVsEXu6cLX1Opj4=)\n[3] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFONECZtuS5VtNttLlHt-tGM4fLbK5rXRpWha9x7spRlWbxJLW7fM1EUTSk11zVmoMsgbJYopeSAFKpXEJ64ZR3b5e64OaNkpsA3XzwME7r0QPKQyjeAqnyPn4=)\n[4] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFgh9gtFFOGtReqt83PBf5blnZWyWEfPTfnlotDBcEmG4cRYBpg5PT-JUlkRRRW2VUQ9SMRXlosRhg1GD2rv6Z9qp141cwOlRFlBXHOlhvceQTiTX15TIj9RHxU91Sl5TyjiHwNgEao6kbf2sb-SNz9ff5UNcb2iLfN00_pPkEaQSi4k_1w1UE-e9z3Si2063HbIWPYlvY=)\n[5] [wordpress.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG6BhjeHxjlgeM9XeZnDH8CUAQjCC_tuHvjBnK7ioN3kucaQIXyKzy8L2Zq_rALNUCXQovdHpx7Cr-CZzgaBRAk5s7zSMtmU-Kg9eNq3QjlKBM5dxwPatS2eo8oktbDYgCCSHjAfDpoHS7Ykg74izlRRxRZqpI1S8FD6Sq0eMc8c31vH6dg1oCfN19w7wThSriztQ==)\n[6] [manimlabs.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEC67FiA7ptOptEVrS8Gu38PJX4N-3ZCpBSYMk-pNYyBwX7-Rmi-R1qO4Gxdy4DYCawrfMTW9saXnhwq2yYPEyP9lJHQJDelB4xiWFZ2BYuIQ==)\n[7] [github.com](https://vertexaisearc